    "body": "Escalated from effort:medium to effort:high. The claim is released.\n\nDone in PR #3737 (draft, `Refs #3560`, branch `issue/3560-heavy-reach`, head `e04cf9f82`):\n- A changed `#[cfg(test)]` module reaches only the `lib` target of its crate. Example: `crates/motion/src/drilling/tests.rs` goes from 95 steps to 3 steps.\n- `src/main.rs` and `src/bin/..` reach only `bins` and the integration binaries of their crate.\n- Each doubt keeps the crate reach.\n- `--dry-run` and the run name each skipped step (`not run: ...`) and print the reached and skipped counts.\n\nNot done: a library file still reaches the whole lane of its crate and of each dependent crate. A per-module `use` graph is not sound without guards. These cases need guards:\n- glob imports and re-exports hide the module path;\n- a trait impl changes each caller of the trait;\n- a method call does not name its module;\n- a registry (`inventory`, `ctor`) runs code that no caller names.\n\nThis is new design under a \"never drop a lane\" rule, so it is above effort:medium. The decision file `docs/decisions/3560-heavy-reach-files.md` records the rule and the dropped options. A next worker can add a new `Seen` variant in `xtask/src/heavy_files.rs`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
